Do not create a new database connection for every query without pooling.

Do not run expensive schema introspection repeatedly when cached metadata is valid.

Do not allow the SQL editor to return an unlimited number of rows or execute unbounded workloads without appropriate policy.

Do not use aggressive polling as the only mechanism when a better notification mechanism is feasible. If polling is used as a fallback, keep it bounded and document its consistency interval.

